# Dead load on a floor and its share

Each layer of the floor is worked out from its thickness and unit weight. The pie chart shows the
same values, and the percentages under it are the shares the chart draws.

## Layers
g_slab: 200 mm * 24 kN/m³ -> kPa | concrete slab
g_screed: 50 mm * 22 kN/m³ -> kPa | screed
g_services: 0.3 kPa | services
g_ceiling: 0.2 kPa | ceiling
g_part: 1 kPa | partitions allowance
G: g_slab + g_screed + g_services + g_ceiling + g_part -> kPa | total dead load

```mermaid
pie showData
  title Dead load, kPa
  "Slab" : 4.8
  "Screed" : 1.1
  "Services" : 0.3
  "Ceiling" : 0.2
  "Partitions" : 1.0
```

## Shares
s_slab: g_slab / G -> % | slab
s_screed: g_screed / G -> % | screed
s_part: g_part / G -> % | partitions
s_rest: (g_services + g_ceiling) / G -> % | services and ceiling
